Chapter: DisjointSlice
  cites Gpu chapter Thread

 A DisjointSlice is a witness-typed parallel-write surface. Access
 requires a ThreadIndex, which is constructible only from hardware
 thread coordinates. This ensures each thread writes to its own
 slot, making parallel writes provably disjoint at the type level.

 We say:

Section: Types

  DisjointSlice = record {
    ds-base : Integer,
    ds-length : Integer
  }

Section: Construction

  disjoint-from-buffer : Integer, Integer -> DisjointSlice
  disjoint-from-buffer (base) (len) =
    DisjointSlice { ds-base = base, ds-length = len }

Section: Access

  disjoint-length : DisjointSlice -> Integer
  disjoint-length (s) = s.ds-length

